## [Searching faces in a collection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/collections.md)

- [Managing face collections, faces, and users](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/managing-face-collections.md): Describes how to manage faces, users, and collections.
- [Using similarity thresholds for associating and matching faces](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/thresholds-collections.md): Describes how to use and calculate similarity thresholds for collection operations.
- [Guidance for indexing faces in common scenarios](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/guidance-index-faces.md): Describes how to use IndexFaces to add faces to a collection in common scenarios
- [Searching for faces and users within a collection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/collections-search-faces.md): Describes how to use IndexFaces to add faces to a collection in common scenarios
- [Use cases that involve public safety](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/considerations-public-safety-use-cases.md): In addition to the recommendations listed in and , you should use the following best practices when deploying face detection and comparison systems in use cases that involve public safety.
- [Creating a collection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/create-collection-procedure.md): You can use the CreateCollection operation to create a collection.
- [Tagging collections](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/tag-collections.md): You can identify, organize, search for, and filter Amazon Rekognition collections by using tags.
- [Listing collections](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/list-collection-procedure.md): You can use the ListCollections operation to list the collections in the region that you are using.
- [Describing a collection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/describe-collection-procedure.md): You can use the DescribeCollection operation to get the following information about a collection:
- [Deleting a collection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/delete-collection-procedure.md): You can use the DeleteCollection operation to delete a collection.
- [Adding faces to a collection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/add-faces-to-collection-procedure.md): You can use the IndexFaces operation to detect faces in an image and add them to a collection.
- [Listing faces and associated users in a collection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/list-faces-in-collection-procedure.md): You can use the ListFaces operation to list faces and their associated users in a collection.
- [Deleting faces from a collection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/delete-faces-procedure.md): You can use the DeleteFaces operation to delete faces from a collection.
- [Creating a user](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/create-user.md): You can use the CreateUser operation to create a new user in a collection using a unique user ID you provide.
- [Deleting a user](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/delete-user.md): You can use the DeleteUser operation to delete a user from a collection, based on the provided UserID.
- [Associating faces to a user](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/associate-faces.md): You can use the AssociateFaces operation to associate multiple individual faces with a single user.
- [Disassociating faces from a user](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/disassociate-faces.md): You can use the DisassociateFaces operation to remove the association between a user ID and a face ID.
- [Listing users in a collection](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/list-users.md): You can use the ListUsers operation to list UserIds and the UserStatus.
- [Searching for a face (face ID)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/search-face-with-id-procedure.md): You can use the SearchFaces operation to search for users in a collection that match the largest face in a supplied image.
- [Searching for a face (image)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/search-face-with-image-procedure.md): You can use the SearchFacesByImage operation to search for faces in a collection that match the largest face in a supplied image.
- [Searching for users (face ID/ user ID)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/search-users.md): You can use the SearchUsers operation to to search for users in a specified collection that match a supplied face ID or user ID.
- [Searching for users (image)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/search-users-by-image.md): SearchUsersByImagesearches the specified CollectionID for users in a collection that match the largest face detected in a supplied image.
- [Searching stored videos for faces](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rekognition/latest/dg/procedure-person-search-videos.md): You can search a collection for faces that match faces of people who are detected in a stored video or a streaming video.

